{
 "manufacturer": "Danfoss",
 "manufacturer_slug": "danfoss",
 "model": "VLT Midi Drive FC 280 (Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "fc-280",
 "short_model": "FC 280",
 "aliases": [
  "FC280",
  "FC-280",
  "VLT Midi Drive FC 280",
  "VLT Midi Drive"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "VLT Midi Drive FC 280 on its built-in RS-485 port with 8-30 Protocol = Modbus RTU and the FC control profile.",
 "summary": "The FC 280 is Danfoss's compact general-purpose (Midi) drive with a built-in RS-485 port that can run Modbus RTU. Control and status words are exchanged as coils (control bits 1-16, status bits 33-48), and every drive parameter is a holding register at ten times its parameter number. This map lists the control/status coils, the communication parameters, the main readouts and the alarm/warning words.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "parameter-derived",
  "note": "Coils and registers are numbered from 1 and sent minus 1 (coil 65 = address 64, register 40001 = address 0). A parameter's register is 10 x its parameter number (16-13 -> 16130) and the request uses that minus 1; the design guide reads 3-03 (register 3030) at register address 3029."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "VLT Midi Drive FC 280 Design Guide (chapter 5 RS485 Installation and Set-up, Modbus RTU)",
  "doc_number": "MG07B302",
  "revision_date": "2017-05",
  "url": "https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG07B302.pdf",
  "pages": "Design Guide printed pp. 60-67 (network settings p. 60, addressing and coil/register tables pp. 61-62, parameter access and examples pp. 63-66, FC profile pp. 66-67). Programming Guide MG07C402 (https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG07C402.pdf, 02/2019): 8-** descriptions printed pp. 78-83, conversion table p. 113, parameter list with conversion index and type pp. 120-131."
 },
 "notes": [
  "32-bit values are high word first: the design guide's example reads 3-03 at registers 3030/3031 and gets 0x0016 0xE360, and its preset-multiple example writes 1-24 = 738 (7.38 A) as 0x0000 0x02E2.",
  "Scale comes from each parameter's conversion index in the programming guide (-1 = x0.1, -2 = x0.01, -3 = x0.001, 0 = x1). Indices 74, 75, 67 and 100 have factors 3600, 3600000, 1/60 and 1 relative to SI units, so 15-00/15-01 arrive in hours, 15-02 in kWh, 16-57 in RPM and 16-34/16-39 in °C (scale 1).",
  "Left out: 16-05 Main Actual Value [%] (normalised N2), 16-09 Custom Readout, 16-62/16-64 analog inputs (unit not given), 16-66 Digital Output (text), 16-67/16-68 pulse inputs and 16-69 pulse output (unit not given), 16-20 Motor Angle, text and array parameters.",
  "The design guide for this drive lists no 50000/50200 control registers; bus control uses coils 1-16 (control word), 17-32 (16-bit speed reference, 4000h = 100 %, negative in two's complement), 33-48 (status word) and 49-64 (output frequency, or feedback in closed loop).",
  "Uint8 parameters are read and written as one 16-bit register.",
  "Bit-by-bit coil names follow the FC profile tables; coil 15 has no function and STW coils 37-39 and 45 are unused."
 ],
